    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2GtzUm5hXcLmjePs7nN39W2)_\n\nThe conflict markers this PR was opened for are already gone from `main` (resolved in the merge of #248), so the doc change is dropped. What is left is one line: `sp-org-tag-groups.el` still has the `@phone` rule that 8b08da2 removed from the doc, which makes the `tangle` check fail for that module. Deleting the line makes the `.el` match the doc.\n\n`tangle` will stay red for two other modules whose docs Sia edited ahead of the `.el` (`sp-search.el`, `sp-org-custom-highlight.el`); not touched here.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCP1EeS4LxrGn5uw6X",
    "changed_files": 1,
    "closed_at": "2026-11-02T14:41:35Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "OWNER",
            "body": "The `tangle` check failed on this PR, and it is also red on `main` (0a9b33d), so it is not caused by the marker fix. It reports three modules that differ from their docs.\n\n- **Fixed here:** `sp-org-tag-groups.el` still had the `@phone` rule that 8b08da2 removed from the doc; I deleted that line to match the doc.\n- **Not touched, still red:** `base/navi/sp-search.el` (the doc dropped the Recoll functions in 8b08da2) and `text/sp-org-custom-highlight.el` (the doc renamed `my-org-insert-inline-comment` to `sp-org-insert-inline-comment`, but its `C-c h` binding still uses the old name, so re-tangling would break the binding). Both come from in-progress edits of yours, so I left them.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
